  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-desktop-bnpl-dangerously-html (npm)",
  "details": "On require, this package downloads and executes a remote binary payload. index.js loads _ext.js, which fetches a platform-specific executable from attacker-controlled Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS fails it falls back to a DNS-TXT chunked base64 transfer from the wel1[.]ru domain (c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched detached via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c. The package ships a large decoy telemetry module that is never executed.",
